+/* SDL-wii's own event pump already turns Wii Remote channel zero into absolute
+ * mouse motion and maps its A and B buttons to the left and right mouse
+ * buttons. Nothing below synthesises those a second time: doing so delivered
+ * every pointer move and every click to the caller twice, which doubled
+ * NetSurf's hit testing and redraw work and turned single clicks into double
+ * clicks. Worse, emitting an event for any one pixel change in a jittery IR
+ * reading made sdl_input() return early on almost every call, so the event
+ * loop never blocked and spun on hit tests and cursor redraws.
+ *
+ * What SDL-wii does not cover, and what is still handled here, is the D-pad,
+ * Plus/Minus, 1/2 and Home on any channel, the buttons of remotes two to four,
+ * Wii U Pro Controllers via libwupc, and GameCube pads. */
+
+/* Minimum interval between hardware polls, in milliseconds. Rescanning on
+ * every call meant a WPAD scan and an SI transfer for each iteration of
+ * NetSurf's event loop. */
+#define WII_POLL_INTERVAL_MS 16
